            <td height="6"> 
              <div align="center"><font size="4" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b><font size="6">Support 
                Radio Intifada</font></b></font></div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="6"> 
              <hr>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="2"> 
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>PMWATCH 
                - August 19, 2002</b> -- In addition to mobilizing criticism against 
                the media and providing the media with access to pro-Palestinian 
                voices, PMWatch is also always actively promoting a greater presence 
                of Palestinian voices in the media. Radio Intifada is such a presence 
                and we urge everyone to help support it.</font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Palestine 
                Media Watch <br>
                (610) 993 - 0608</font>
              </p><hr>
              <p>D<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">ear Friends 
                and all supporters of justice, </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> To those 
                from the Arab and Muslim American communities, I urge you to support 
                this program and Pacificas KPFK station fund drive in Los Angeles. 
                We shouldn't limit ourselves to criticizing the distortions of 
                main stream media about Arab and Islamic cultures and issues. 
                We must be pro-active and support alternative voices. Radio Intifada 
                is a genuine program that strives to bring the authentic voices 
                of the peoples of the regions of West/South Asia and North Africa. 
                </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> And for non 
                Arab, non-Muslim, Americans, I urge you to strongly support this 
                program, which is offering a rare opportunity to learn the stories 
                and issues directly from people belonging to these regions and 
                organically connected to its progressive issues. Radio Intifada 
                is produced by volunteers who among them have immigrants from 
                the regions it is covering. </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Please listen 
                and pledge money to help the station sustain such an alternative 
                quality programming. Listen to our Palestine program below and 
                you'll find out what we are talking about. </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> In solidarity, 
                Michel Shehadeh shehadeh@pacbell.net </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Radio Intifada 
                ....Voices from Calcutta to Casablanca </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Palestine 
                Wed, August 21st @ 3 p.m., KPFK 90.7 FM </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                By popular demand, this program on Palestine, which launched the 
                West/South Asia and North Africa Collectives Radio Intifada, 
                will be re-broadcast August 21, during the Mini-Fund Drive. </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                You will hear - </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Dr. Salman Abu Sitta, who has done ground breaking demographic 
                research establishing the viability of the Palestinians right 
                of return </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Kayan, a teenager from Deheheishe Refugee camp outside Bethlehem 
                who was touring the US </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Eileen Kuttab, long time Palestinian womens movement activist 
                and professor of womens studies at Birzeit University </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                The poetry of Mahmoud Darwish </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                The music of Marcel Khalife and Sabreen. </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Hosted by Michel Shehadeh </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Co-produced by </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Hagit Borer, Armineh Ebrahimian, Sherna Gluck and Michel Shehadeh 
                with technical support from Esther Manilla and Eben Ray </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Listen - Call in - Subscribe - and show your support for Radio 
                Intifada. </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Special Pledge Offers include: </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Ali on Broadway CD (Lebanese artist fusing ME music and jazz) 
                </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                Current issue and one year back copies of Al Jadid, Quarterly 
                Review of Arab Culture and Arts </font>
              </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                A CD of any back programs of Radio Intifada and a limited number 
                of copies of the book, An American Feminist in Palestine: the 
                Intifada Years- (first one), by Sherna Berger Gluck </font>
              </p><p align="center"> 
            </p></td>
